# Drafted by Gemini (R13 raum), edited.

~ prefight
Narrator: Black feathers drift through the dry cornstalks, smelling of cold ash and old tallow. At the heart of the circle, the great crow tilts its ragged head.
raum [sly]: Look how plump with little shames you came, all ripe for the picking. Pay the toll, children, and let old Raum shuck you clean.
* [if flag.song_known] Sing the song we learned -> sing
* Say our secrets are ours -> defy
* Attack -> fight

~ sing
Narrator: As the old tune rises, the brass banjo strings inside the beast's gullet hum in answer, and Raum's heavy wings falter out of time.
raum [angry]: Hush that racket, you tin-eared thieves, that tune is swallowed and mine to keep!
set raum_song_sung
-> fight

~ defy
raum [sly]: Keep them tucked beneath your ribs, then. They taste all the sweeter when I crack the bone to get the marrow.
-> fight

~ fight
set fw_raum_started
combat fw_raum
-> END

~ jericho_farewell
if not quest.fields_of_the_crow >= raum
quest fields_of_the_crow raum
endif
set raum_slain
Narrator: Black feathers scatter like soot, leaving a pale, lantern-bright figure cradling an old banjo as the red stain fades from the moon above.
jericho_sticks [smile]: Well now, that is a mighty fine breath of night air after so long in the dark. You folks carried my tune right through the briars.
* Ask him to rest -> jericho_rest
* Ask about the song -> jericho_song
* Bid him farewell -> jericho_go

~ jericho_rest
jericho_sticks [weary]: My straw is long gone to ash, friend, and these old fingers have played their last reel. When the last chord fades, I reckon I will drift on easy.
-> jericho_farewell

~ jericho_song
jericho_sticks [smile]: I wrote "Virgil's Birdcage" for a little blackbird that would not sing behind wire. A secret kept in fear is just another cage, and you broke the lock.
-> jericho_farewell

~ jericho_go
jericho_sticks [smile]: Keep each other warm on the road back to Wickermoor, travelers. May the corn grow tall and the crows keep their distance.
set jericho_at_rest
-> END

~ coming_home
set fw_home
Narrator: Back in the smoky square of Foxwillow, the surviving scarecrows split at the seams as living folk stumble out blinking, while burned husks lie still in the dirt.
martha_langtree [weary]: God forgive us for what we let fester behind locked doors. Those poor souls we burned in our madness will never walk out of the straw.
jonah_sawyer [sad]: I set the torch to my own neighbors, thinking them monsters. I will spend the rest of my nights mending what I broke.
william_lodge [weary]: Get your people under a roof, Martha, and tend the living while you can. Come on, friends, let us ride back to Wickermoor before the frost settles.
quest fields_of_the_crow done
set act2_done += 1
# Act II raises the party four levels, 4 to 8, whichever chapters they are (plan 5.1): the fifth chapter done gives none.
if flag.act2_done <= 4
xp milestone
endif
set sister_rain_invited
set adela_painting_bats
-> END
